arcs:
Grand go the years in the crescent above them;
Worlds scoop their arcs, and firmaments row,
Diadems drop and Doges surrender,

architect's:
The Dean is in the Chapter House;
He is reading the architect's bill
For the completed restoration of the Cathedral.

archangels:
Seraphs fall before Thee,
Angels and Archangels,
Cherub throngs adore Thee;

Still light was poured on him, more light;
Angels, Archangels he outstripped
Exultant in exceeding might,

archangel's:
No daybreak can bestir;
The slow archangel's syllables
Must awaken her.
